From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:28:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 101/144] GreatDANE: privacy docs: update-check declaration
 pending server-log answer; GMP diagnostics not opt-in (NGD R2-M1 per ruling,
 L6)

- PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md and the PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy comment:
  - Removed the unproven "used only to answer the request" wording.
  - Declaration and retention for the pepecoin.surf update check are marked PENDING the server-log answer
    (now owned by Curb Appeal), with the plan for each outcome (logged: OtherDiagnosticData, not linked, not
    tracking, AppFunctionality, plus Analytics only if used to count installs; off or anonymized: undeclared,
    with the log setting recorded).
  - Noted that the DisableAppUpdate policy stops the check (UpdateServiceStub.sys.mjs:209-215).
- L6: OtherDiagnosticData is no longer described as opt-in only. The default-on GMP update check to
  aus5.mozilla.org (media.gmp-manager.url, all.js:3474; firefox.js:2378/2400/2448) sends version, build ID,
  build target (OS + arch), locale, channel and OS version. The manifest values are unchanged.
- grokipedia.com uses our own letter tile (noted).
- README: round-3 signing notes (DANE_ARCH allowlist, no dmg overwrite, wider owner guard, ad-hoc mode, legacy
  --deep guard).
